{{/*
  on-call/shared/prior-reports — treats the daily CSO report folder (ReportsDir,
  written one-file-per-day by "On-Call: watch and summarize") as a shared
  knowledge base of past incidents, reused across the On-Call group so triage
  and playbook-authoring can learn from prior art.

  The block is emitted ONLY when the folder actually exists on disk
  (`DirExists`); when ReportsDir is unset or points at a nonexistent path the
  fragment renders to nothing, so callers keep their previous behaviour with no
  extra guards of their own.

  Two modes select the wording (the DirExists gate is identical in both):

    - "search"  — for an incident coordinator ("On-Call: I have been paged").
                  Emits a "### Consult prior CSO reports" step that spawns ONE
                  child conversation to mine ReportsDir for similar past
                  incidents and report the matching solutions back via the
                  standard child-report mechanism.
    - "consult" — for a maintenance/authoring prompt ("On-Call: update
                  investigation instructions") that must NOT spawn children.
                  Emits an inline instruction to read the past reports directly
                  for investigation *technique* (useful queries, dashboards,
                  common pitfalls) while updating the playbook.

  Usage — pass the full prompt context plus the resolved folder and mode:

      {{ template "on-call/shared/prior-reports"
           (dict "Ctx" . "ReportsDir" $reportsDir "Mode" "search") }}
*/ -}}
{{- $ctx := .Ctx -}}
{{- $reportsDir := .ReportsDir -}}
{{- $mode := .Mode -}}
{{- if and $reportsDir (DirExists $reportsDir) -}}
{{- if eq $mode "search" }}
### Consult prior CSO reports for similar incidents

A folder of past daily CSO reports exists at `{{ $reportsDir }}` (one
`YYYY-MM-DD.md` file per calendar day, written by `On-Call: watch and
summarize`). These reports are prior art: a symptom you are triaging now may
have been seen — and mitigated — before. Mine them **in a child conversation**
so this step runs in parallel with the ingest/decomposition work and does not
block the coordinator.

Spawn one prior-art searcher (reuse an **idle** existing child —
`{{ Default "(none)" $ctx.Children.MCPText }}` — if one matches; otherwise
create fresh):

`mitto_conversation_new(self_id: "{{ $ctx.Session.ID }}", title: "Search prior CSO reports", initial_prompt: <see below>)`.

The searcher's initial prompt MUST:

- State the current incident's title and the strongest symptom signals from the
  ingest pass (affected services, error signatures, dashboards, timeline
  window) so it knows what to match against.
- Instruct it to enumerate `{{ $reportsDir }}/*.md` (the daily reports), read
  the most relevant ones (prefer recent + keyword-matched files; it does **not**
  need to read every file), and identify past incidents whose **symptoms,
  affected services, or root causes** overlap the current one.
- For each match, extract: the report date/file, the matching symptoms, the
  identified root cause (if any), and — most importantly — the
  **solution / mitigation that was applied** and whether it worked.
- Be honest: report "no similar prior incident found" rather than forcing a weak
  match. Do NOT propose or execute any mitigation itself — it only surfaces
  prior art for the coordinator to weigh.
- Report back via
  `mitto_children_tasks_report(self_id: <own id>, task_id: "prior-reports", status: "completed" | "partial" | "failed", summary: "<N matches / none>", details: "<per-match: file, symptoms, root cause, applied solution, outcome, report link>")`.

Do not block the whole flow on this searcher. Collect its findings when you
synthesize (Step 5 / round-1 synthesis) by including its conversation id in the
`mitto_children_tasks_wait` call alongside the investigators, and fold any
matching prior solution into the ranked hypotheses as **corroborating prior
art** (clearly labelled as historical, not a current finding).
{{- else if eq $mode "consult" }}
### Consult prior CSO reports for investigation technique

A folder of past daily CSO reports exists at `{{ $reportsDir }}` (one
`YYYY-MM-DD.md` file per calendar day, written by `On-Call: watch and
summarize`). Before writing the auto-generated sections, **read a sample of
these reports directly in this conversation** (do NOT spawn a child — this is an
authoring task). Prefer the most recent files and any whose incidents resemble
the source material you just gathered.

Mine them for *how the team actually investigated*, and let that shape the
investigation instructions you write:

- **Useful queries & dashboards** — the specific Splunk/Grafana/Datadog queries,
  dashboard links, or log filters that repeatedly proved decisive.
- **Effective techniques** — diagnostic steps that consistently narrowed the
  root cause fast (e.g. "check CoreDNS resolution latency first for 5xx spikes").
- **Common pitfalls** — false leads, misleading signals, or dead-ends that
  recurred across incidents, so the playbook can warn future investigators.
- **Recurring failure modes** — symptom → root-cause patterns seen more than
  once; these deserve a dedicated playbook section.

Incorporate these as concrete guidance in the auto-generated block (attributing
"observed across past reports in `{{ $reportsDir }}`" where useful). If the
folder holds no relevant reports, skip this silently — do not fabricate
techniques.
{{- end }}
{{- end -}}
